From 36daee1a836ffc7c7e1dbc89a62e2ed0014146de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dev <dev@example.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 11:37:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Visual polish: max-flash, theming, condensed cards, quest
 popout

- Purchase/upgrade feedback: toasts now pop with a golden flash, and maxing
  out an upgrade or vendor triggers a 'Fully upgraded' card flash with a
  star-poof burst (UpgradesPanel.tsx, Toast.tsx, app.css).
- Reflavoured the Alchemist and Enchanter permanent upgrades to fit their
  vendor (Alchemical Assay, Restorative Tinctures, Runic Insight, Enchanted
  Seal) and brightened the washed-out Holy skin swatch (progression.ts).
- Fixed the samurai sprite sitting up-and-left of center via a per-class
  display offset (HeroSprite.tsx).
- Base text size default raised to 135%, card titles/tags bigger, quest
  titles bigger still (settings.ts, app.css).
- Quest board cards are now clickable and open a full-detail popout
  (QuestPanel.tsx).
- Hero cards are condensed to a summary row by default, expandable per-hero
  for the full stat/mods/injury/livery breakdown (HeroesPanel.tsx).
- Fixed the desktop companion drag region: unlocking previously still could
  not be dragged because the sprite/plate area force-set no-drag over the
  whole visible window; only interactive buttons keep no-drag now (app.css).
- Added a theme-aware background to the idle companion's info plate so
  light themes (Old Parchment, the new Daylight) are legible over the
  desktop instead of using a hardcoded dark tint (app.css).
- Added a 'Daylight' theme (near-white, Windows-like) alongside the
  existing High Contrast dark theme (settings.ts).
- Added a Style setting: 'Adventure' (unchanged) vs 'Modern', a rounded
  pill/soft-card overlay driven entirely by CSS, no component changes
  required (settings.ts, SettingsPanel.tsx, app.css).
